    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to note AB in our formula rate tariff, our revenue requirement includes the amortization of any net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes resulting from changes to income tax laws, income tax rates (including changes in apportionment) and other actions taken by a taxing authority.
          <br/>
          <br/>We have a net deficient deferred income tax regulatory asset as a result of the 2011 Michigan Corporate Income tax change. This deficient deferred income tax regulatory asset is amortized based on the remaining book lives of the property giving rise to the net deferred income tax. The amortization of the Michigan CIT (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is $125,761. We also have a net (excess)/deferred income tax regulatory liability resulting from the implementation of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017. The amortization of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017 net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is $(2,424,851).
          <br/>
          <br/>The total net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax amortization of $(2,299,090) is reported as the input to page 3, line 24a in our formula rate tariff.
        </span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
