    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">We have a net excess deferred income tax regulatory liability resulting from the implementation of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017. 
          <br/>
          <br/>We use RSGM for the amortization of the (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes to customers. The deferred taxes associated with public utility plant property will be amortized over a period ranging from 3 to 65 years and deferred taxes not related to public utility property will be amortized over a period of 32 years.
          <br/>
          <br/>The total net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax amortization of $(2,299,090), discussed further in the note shown on page 232, is reported as the input to page 3, line 24a in our formula rate tariff.
        </span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
