    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The activity also reflects prior year adjustments to actual, and certain tax year 2024 payments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other taxes primarily includes Sales and Use tax, City tax, Federal Highway Use tax, and other taxes and also includes certain activity related to 2024.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Payroll taxes are paid by ITC Holdings Corp. to the various governmental agencies and allocated to its subsidiaries including ITC Transmission.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Federal income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">State income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total other tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 18, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total property tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 16, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total payroll tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 13, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The 'Other Accounts' balance represents preliminary charges in account 183 for future capital projects, charges for certain political and related activities in accounts 426.4 and certain warehouse related labor expenses in account 163.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC&#8217;s Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental Amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC's Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amounts shown as transfers in column (f) from account 391 were solely for the purpose of implementing FERC Order 898 and represent transfers of computer hardware, software and communication equipment to newly established plant accounts 351.1, 351.2, 351.3, 397.1, 397.2, 397.3.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amount represents balances previously recorded to account 397 prior to implementation of FERC Order 898.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This amount represents capitalized depreciation for vehicles and equipment used in the construction process.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Net accumulated depreciation related to reserve adjustments pursuant to a Commission approved depreciation study on docket #ER22-2-000, December 1, 2021</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The depreciation rates shown in column (e) are straight line rates which when applied to monthly plant balances, will uniformly recover the unrecovered cost, adjusted for net salvage, over the remaining life of the plant.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Average Remaining Life shown in column (g) is based on the latest approved depreciation study, which is based on balances as of December 31, 2020.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In addition to depreciation provided by application of reported rates, the 2025 provision for depreciation was reduced in the amount of $1,321,799 for certain general plant accounts, persuant to implementing the results of the 2021 depreciation study approved by the Commission on December 1, 2021, in docket #ER22-2-000</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Page 422, Columns (f) and (g): All lengths are in circuit miles.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-54" id="fn-54" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Contains plant co-owned by the Michigan Public Power Agency, which is not an associated company. See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant / Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-55" id="fn-55" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Contains plant co-owned by Michigan Electric Transmission Company, LLC, which is an associated company.&#160; See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant / Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-57" id="fn-57" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-58" id="fn-58" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-59" id="fn-59" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Network load is populated on Schedule 9 on page 400. No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available (other than Schedule 9) and is maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-60" id="fn-60" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use MISO as billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-61" id="fn-61" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITCTransmission does not report &#8220;Number of Units&#8221; in columns (b), (c),(e) and (f): rather it only reports the total dollars. The quantity is not readily available and information pertaining to the amounts sold and purchased are maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-62" id="fn-62" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is reported in columns (e) &#8211; (j) as such information is maintained by MISO as the billing agent and not readily available. However, network load is reported in column (b).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-63" id="fn-63" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Transmission is a transmission only company and as such, Monthly Energy and Sales for Resale information is not applicable.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-64" id="fn-64" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The First Mortgage Bonds listed were issued under our first mortgage and deed of trust and secured by a first mortgage lien on substantially all of our property.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-65" id="fn-65" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">During the year ended December 31, 2025, we borrowed $426,700,000 and repaid $318,300,000 under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-66" id="fn-66" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-67" id="fn-67" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents issuance of long-term debt of $150,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $326,500,000.</link:footnote>
